on of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{2}-3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{2}-3x) & =x({x}^{2}-3x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-3x)-({x}^{2}-3x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x)+4({x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =x({x}^{2}-3x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-3)-({x}^{2}-3x)(2x-3)+4({x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =x({x}^{2}-3x)\\cdot 2-({x}^{2}-3x)(2x-3)+4({x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{2}-9x+4{x}^{2}-12x \\\\  & =7{x}^{2}-21x \\\\  & =7x(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420952 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1069 "q-337842" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1071 "Given that $D=3{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=x-5?$" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1072 #uuid "fbf85b19-bc66-596e-8aa5-463e28e677ea" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420955 1074 "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=3{x}^{2},{f}_{1}=-x,$ and ${f}_{0}=-2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(x-5) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2)(x-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(x-5)-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-5)-2(x-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\cdot 0-x\\cdot 1-2x+10 \\\\  & =10-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420956 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420960 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420956 1062 #uuid "2788ab1a-6e0a-5a50-87b3-604347a0ca06" 13194139534423 17592186045417 true] [17592186420956 1063 #edb/ref 17592